# CompTIA A+ — Troubleshooting

What is step 1 of the CompTIA troubleshooting methodology?
---
Identify the problem
= identify problem
---
The full order: identify the problem, establish a theory, test the theory, plan and implement, verify and prevent, document.

In the troubleshooting methodology, what comes right after testing the theory?
---
Establish a plan of action
= plan of action
= establish a plan
= establish a plan of action and implement the solution
---
Then implement it, verify full functionality with preventive measures, and document everything.

What is the final step of the troubleshooting methodology?
---
Document findings, actions, and outcomes
= document
= documentation
= document findings
---
The step everyone skips. Next time the fix takes minutes instead of hours.

Name the six steps of the CompTIA troubleshooting methodology
---
quota: 6
attempts: 9
+ Identify the problem
= identify
+ Establish a theory of probable cause
= establish a theory
= theory
+ Test the theory
= test
+ Establish a plan of action and implement the solution
= plan of action
= implement
+ Verify full system functionality
= verify
+ Document findings, actions, and outcomes
= document

Name the seven laser printer imaging steps
---
quota: 7
attempts: 10
+ Processing
+ Charging
+ Exposing
+ Developing
+ Transferring
+ Fusing
+ Cleaning
---
In that order. The fuser melts the toner onto the page, which is why fresh prints are warm.

A laser-printed page smears when touched. Which component has failed?
---
fuser
= the fuser
= fuser assembly
= fuser unit
---
The fuser's heat and pressure bond toner to paper. No fusing, no bond.

Repeated marks appear at regular intervals down every laser-printed page. What is the likely cause?
---
a damaged drum
= drum
= the drum
= imaging drum
= a damaged roller
= dirty roller
---
The drum's circumference sets the repeat distance. A scratch or debris prints once per rotation.

A PC powers on but shows nothing, and emits a pattern of beeps. What is the beeping?
---
a POST beep code
= POST beep code
= beep code
= POST code
= POST error
---
The BIOS reporting a hardware fault it found before video works. The pattern's meaning is board-specific.

The system clock resets every time a PC is unplugged. What should be replaced?
---
the CMOS battery
= CMOS battery
= motherboard battery
= CR2032
---
The coin cell that keeps the real-time clock running without power.

An LCD shows an image so dim it is only visible under a flashlight. What has failed?
---
the backlight
= backlight
= backlight or inverter
= inverter
---
The panel is still drawing the image. On old CCFL panels the inverter powering the lamp is the usual culprit.

A PC intermittently reboots under heavy load. What is the most likely hardware cause?
---
overheating
= thermal
= heat
= CPU overheating
= failing power supply
= PSU
---
Check fans, heat sink dust, and thermal paste first, then the PSU under load.

Windows shows a spinning cursor and 100% disk usage on an old laptop with a hard drive. What upgrade helps most?
---
replace the hard drive with an SSD
= SSD
= an SSD
= install an SSD
= upgrade to SSD
---
A spinning disk at 100% is the classic bottleneck. An SSD is the single largest perceived speedup.

A phone's battery drains fast and the case has begun to bulge. What should the user do?
---
stop using it and replace the battery
= replace the battery
= stop using it
= battery replacement
---
A swollen lithium battery is a fire risk. Do not puncture it, and recycle it properly.
